                <pb facs="0754" n="656" xml:id="pg656"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2917: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-11T13:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                                1920—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 11—9:49
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>413. Your 295 July 29,10 p.m. Japanese Foreign Office states that views of
                    Japanese Government on proposed representations to China in connection with
                    payment of Hukuang Tientsin-Pukow Railway coupons are as expressed in my 337,
                    July 11, noon [<hi rendition="#italic">10 a.m.</hi>], and that the Japanese
                    Minister at Peking was notified of his Government’s views and was instructed at
                    that time that when the matter should come before the Ministers in China of the
                    interested powers he should in harmony with them take such action as might be
                    proper in the circumstances. Repeated to Peking together with my 337, July 11,
                    noon [<hi rendition="#italic">10 a.m.</hi>].</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
